# Reviewed semantic exceptions. Hash-bound static findings are stored in native_stub_dispositions.json.
# Entries are rule-specific and may not suppress a new field or a changed implementation.
EXEMPT(camera, GetCameraState, S3, useTable, The native result always contains structured camera fields; useTable selects only a Lua table shape.)
EXEMPT(camera, SetCameraTarget, S4, success, Operation acknowledgement after the validated engine side effect; failure is represented by the error pointer. This does not waive side-effect regression tests.)
EXEMPT(camera, WorldToScreenCoords, S4, valid, The native valid flag is true after successful camera projection; readiness failure reports an error.)
EXEMPT(config, SetConfigFloat, S4, success, Operation acknowledgement after the validated engine side effect; failure is represented by the error pointer. This does not waive side-effect regression tests.)
EXEMPT(config, SetConfigInt, S4, success, Operation acknowledgement after the validated engine side effect; failure is represented by the error pointer. This does not waive side-effect regression tests.)
EXEMPT(config, SetConfigString, S4, success, Operation acknowledgement after the validated engine side effect; failure is represented by the error pointer. This does not waive side-effect regression tests.)
EXEMPT(config, SetLogSectionFilterLevel, S4, success, Operation acknowledgement after the validated engine side effect; failure is represented by the error pointer. This does not waive side-effect regression tests.)
EXEMPT(display, HaveAdvShading, S4, enabled, Lua returns true as its first value; HaveAdvShadingFull exposes the independent ground shading state without changing the legacy result layout.)
EXEMPT(display, HaveAdvShading, S5, function, Lua returns true as its first value; HaveAdvShadingFull exposes the independent ground shading state without changing the legacy result layout.)
EXEMPT(effects_control, SpawnSFX, S3, damage, Lua also ignores radius and damage; UnitScript.EmitSfx determines the actual effect parameters.)
EXEMPT(effects_control, SpawnSFX, S3, radius, Lua also ignores radius and damage; UnitScript.EmitSfx determines the actual effect parameters.)
EXEMPT(feature_defs, GetFeatureDefByID, S4, info.resurrectAs, A shared FeatureDef has no resurrection unit identity; null is explicit. Features.GetFeatureResurrect queries the per-instance identity.)
EXEMPT(game, GetAllyTeamStartBox, S4, exists, exists becomes true only after a valid ally-team lookup; invalid IDs return false through result initialization.)
EXEMPT(game_config, SetExperienceGrade, S5, function, The setter writes globalUnitParams by member assignment; its status literals acknowledge those writes.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextHeight, S3, options, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; height is normalized text height and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextHeight, S3, size, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; height is normalized text height and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextHeight, S3, x, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; height is normalized text height and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextHeight, S3, y, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; height is normalized text height and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextWidth, S3, options, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; width is normalized text width and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextWidth, S3, size, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; width is normalized text width and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextWidth, S3, x, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; width is normalized text width and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, FontGetTextWidth, S3, y, The shared font draw query contains position, size and draw options; width is normalized text width and only text and font are relevant.)
EXEMPT(gfx, GetGlobalTexCoords, S4, pageNum, The global texture atlas has one page; Lua returns only UV coordinates and the native-only page index is zero.)
EXEMPT(gfx, GetScreenViewTrans, S4, x, Lua returns a file-static zero vector that is never written; preserve its established semantics.)
EXEMPT(gfx, GetScreenViewTrans, S4, y, Lua returns a file-static zero vector that is never written; preserve its established semantics.)
EXEMPT(gfx, GetScreenViewTrans, S4, z, Lua returns a file-static zero vector that is never written; preserve its established semantics.)
EXEMPT(gfx, GetScreenViewTrans, S5, function, Lua returns a file-static zero vector that is never written; preserve its established semantics.)
EXEMPT(gfx, MatrixDataFromProjectilesVBO, S3, teamID, The projectile matrix query shares the unit matrix descriptor; teamID is a unit-only filter.)
EXEMPT(ground_decals, GetGroundDecalUserData, S4, values[3], Engine decal user data is float3; the fourth element of the existing native float[4] result is zero padding.)
EXEMPT(math_extra, Sgn, S5, function, This is a piecewise-constant mathematical sign function selected by the input; the distinct -1, 0 and 1 branches are its implementation.)
EXEMPT(profiling, GetLuaMemUsage, S4, handleAllocedKB, Native modules have no Lua handle heap. Handle allocation fields are zero; global Lua allocation fields still report actual state.)
EXEMPT(profiling, GetLuaMemUsage, S4, handleAllocsK, Native modules have no Lua handle heap. Handle allocation fields are zero; global Lua allocation fields still report actual state.)
EXEMPT(projectiles, GetPieceProjectileParams, S4, params.gravity.x, Engine gravity acts on the vertical Y axis; horizontal X/Z components are zero.)
EXEMPT(projectiles, GetPieceProjectileParams, S4, params.gravity.z, Engine gravity acts on the vertical Y axis; horizontal X/Z components are zero.)
EXEMPT(projectiles, GetProjectileDamages, S3, tag, Native results include all damage tags together; the Lua tag selector changes only the selected return shape.)
EXEMPT(projectiles, GetProjectileGravity, S4, gravity.x, Engine gravity acts on the vertical Y axis; horizontal X/Z components are zero.)
EXEMPT(projectiles, GetProjectileGravity, S4, gravity.z, Engine gravity acts on the vertical Y axis; horizontal X/Z components are zero.)
